## Dynatrace’s SRE Agent shows evidence behind incident recommendations

Source: Dynatrace — https://www.dynatrace.com/news/blog/the-sre-agent-is-generally-available-investigation-and-triage-start-the-moment-a-problem-is-detected/
Published: 2026-11-11
Channel: news

Dynatrace’s SRE Agent is an incident-investigation agent that works inside configurable operational workflows. Its general-availability announcement focuses on the delay between an alert and understanding what failed, who is affected and which team should respond. Dynatrace says the agent exposes supporting evidence and what it checked and ruled out.

First, Dynatrace identifies a problem and its root cause. The agent starts from that finding, then examines related logs, events, deployments and metrics, follows service dependencies and checks earlier problems. It returns an analysis, affected services and users, and remediation recommendations. The workflow applies configured urgency rules and ownership data to decide where the result goes.

Operators can annotate a problem, open a ticket, notify a team or prepare a proposed fix for approval. The announcement separates the agent’s investigation from the workflow’s defined triggers and subsequent actions. It recommends starting with owned services and critical problems, comparing the analysis with the team’s own findings, and widening the scope after review. Claims about investigations completing within minutes are vendor claims; the illustrative checkout incident is not an independently verified production result.

Why it matters: For teams adopting investigation agents: compare recommendations with their cited evidence and keep consequential fixes behind the intended approval step.

